## Key Observations

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="background:#FEF2F2;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;"><strong>IGAAP vs IFRS PAT divergence</strong></span> — Statutory IGAAP PAT for H1FY26 is a <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">loss of ₹126.71 cr</span>, while IFRS-basis PAT for the same period is a <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">profit of ₹131.72 cr</span>. The ~₹258 cr swing reflects differing treatment under the two accounting frameworks (e.g., premium recognition, reserving, deferred acquisition cost capitalization under IFRS 17 vs IGAAP).
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<strong>Combined ratio above 100%</strong> — At <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">114.13%</span> (IGAAP), the combined ratio indicates underwriting losses on a statutory basis for H1FY26, driven by a <strong>74.28%</strong> claims ratio and <strong>38.40%</strong> EoM ratio.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #22C55E;background:#F0FDF4;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="background:#F0FDF4;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;"><strong>Solvency comfortably above regulatory minimum</strong></span> — Solvency ratio of <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">2.85x</span> remains well above the IRDAI-mandated minimum of 1.50x, indicating adequate capital buffer despite the IGAAP underwriting loss.
</div>

## Notes & Discrepancies Flagged for Transparency

- **GWP cross-check:** The statutory filing's "Gross Premiums Written" YTD Sep-2025 (₹3,47,497 lakh = ₹3,474.97 cr, with 1/n) reconciles almost exactly with the deck's "with 1/n" Total GWP of ₹3,475.0 cr — confirming consistency across sources on the statutory basis. The deck separately shows a "without 1/n" GWP of ₹3,982.7 cr, deliberately excluded per basis-consistency instructions.
- **Retail health GWP:** Only available "with 1/n" (statutory) in the deck's KPI table (₹2,371.8 cr); the "without 1/n" figure (₹2,809.9 cr) was excluded.
- **Commission ratio — not disclosed:** Neither the statutory Reg. 33/52 filing's Analytical Ratios section nor the IR deck discloses a standalone commission ratio. Only Net Commission in absolute terms (₹539.64 cr YTD) is stated, alongside the explicit Combined/Claims/EoM ratios. Per instructions, this line item was left blank rather than derived or estimated, and has been removed from the table above.
- **Net worth cross-check:** Summing statutory filing components — Paid-up Equity (₹1,846.00 cr) + Reserves & Surplus (₹1,109.96 cr) + Fair Value Change A/c (₹6.83 cr) — yields ≈₹2,962.79 cr, modestly higher (~₹6.8 cr, ~0.2%) than the deck's explicitly labeled Net Worth of ₹2,956.0 cr. This is likely a minor presentation/rounding or component-scope difference between the two disclosures; the deck's explicit figure was used per sourcing priority.
- **PAT (IFRS) precision:** Management commentary rounds this to "₹132 crore," but the precise IFRS P&L statement figure (Profit for the period, 6 months ended Sep 30, 2025) is **₹131.72 cr** (₹13,172 lakh) — this precise statement figure was used in the table.
- **Document #4 (Certificate-Regulation-quarter-ended-Sep-2025.pdf):** Upon full read, this was confirmed to be a Reg. 74(5) SEBI Depositories certificate concerning dematerialized share transfers — **not** a solvency ratio certification. No separate solvency-specific certificate was found on the IR page; the solvency ratio (2.85x) was instead sourced from the Analytical Ratios section of the statutory Reg. 33/52 results filing, which is the authoritative disclosure for this metric.
- **Document #5 (investor-relations.aspx):** Reviewed but the current listing shows only FY26-27 filings (subsequent to this period) and older FY24-25 announcements — no separate NL-1/NL-2 IRDAI public disclosure PDFs for Sep-2025 were found distinct from the main statutory results filing (#1), which already embeds the IRDAI-mandated Analytical Ratios (per Regulation 33/52 read with IRDAI circular IRDA/F&A/CIR/LFTD/027/01/2017).</ans>
