Times | 2.55x | 3.03x | 2.25x | 2.85x |\n| Assets Under Management | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 5,458.2 | 8,175.1 | 5,965.2 | 8,481.8 |\n| Yield on Total Investments (Annualized) | % | 7.1% | 7.4% | 7.5% | 7.3% |\n\nW.e.f. October 1, 2024 Long-term products are accounted on 1/n, as mandated by IRDAI, hence FY2025 & H1'FY2026 numbers are not comparable with prior periods\n<sup>1</sup>No reinsurance accepted so \u201cGWP = GDPI\u201d ; <sup>2</sup>Expense of management is calculated without 1/n ; <sup>3</sup> Return on Average Net Worth is not annualized for H1\u2019FY2025 & H1'FY2026\n\n---\n\n## Key Performance Indicators (3/3)\n\n| Particulars | Unit | FY2024 | FY2025 (with 1/n) | H1'FY2025 | H1'FY2026 (with 1/n) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Retail Health GWP | (\u20b9 in Crores) | 3,839.7 | 4,432.5 | 2,201.3 | 2,371.8 |\n| Retail Health Market Share | % | 9.1% | 9.4% | 9.9% | 9.9% |\n| Retail Health Accretion Market Share | % | 12.9% | 11.6% | 15.6% | 9.2% |\n| Number of Active Lives Insured at the end of the Fiscal | (# in Millions) | 14.7 | 20.8 | 17.8 | 23.1 |\n| Network Hospitals | # | 10,460 | 10,421 | 10,190 | 10,507 |\n| % of Cashless Claims through Network Hospitals | % | 70.0% | 72.2% | 73.9% | 71.8% |\n| Claims Settlement Ratio | % | 91.9% | 92.4% | 92.3% | 94.6% |\n| GWP Contribution of New Retail Health Indemnity Policies with Sum Insured >= \u20b9 1 million | % | 70.7% | 74.5% | 74.1% | 81.1% |\n| Avg. Ticket size per policy | \u20b9 | 28,797 | 30,252 | 30,839 | 27,079 |\n| GWP per policy sold by Agents | \u20b9 | 25,028 | 23,233 | 25,108 | 21,859 |\n\n---\n\n## 1 Building a Granular, Growth Oriented and Profitable Health Insurance Franchise\n\n**Product Mix**\n\n**Retail Health GWP & Market Share**\n\n(\u20b9 in Crores)\n\n| Category | Retail Health (By GWP, %) | Group Health (By GWP, %) | PA & Travel (By GWP, %) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2024 | 68.5 | 29.5 | 2.0 |\n| FY2025 | 65.5 | 32.3 | 2.2 |\n| H1'FY2025 | 67.9 | 29.7 | 2.4 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 68.3 | 30.2 | 1.6 |\n\n| Category | Retail Health GWP (\u20b9 in Crores) | Retail Health Market Share (%) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2024 | 3839.7 | 9.1 |\n| FY2025 | 4432.5 | 9.4 |\n| H1'FY2025 | 2201.3 | 9.9 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 2371.8 | 9.9 |\n\n---\n\n## Comprehensive Portfolio of Innovative Health Insurance Products Across All Stages 2 of the Customer Lifecycle\n\n**WELLNESS FOCUSED** ReAssure GoActive\nReAssure 2.0\nReAssure 3.0\n\n**DISEASE MANAGEMENT** smart HEALTH\nReAssure 3.0\n\nHEALTH AGE\n\nniva Health Insurance\n\nSALES PROCESS INCOME\n\n**EMBEDDED** smart HEALTH Xpress Health HEALTH PLUS\n\n**ADVISORY** Travel Assure **All Retail Products HEALTH PLUS**\n\n**MILLENNIALS** Aspire elixir\n\n**SENIOR CITIZEN** SENIOR FIRST\n\n**MASS MARKET** Rise **TIERED NETWORK** <u><strong>RIDER</strong></u>\n\n**MASS AFFLUENT HEALTH PULSE**\n\n**AFFLUENT** ReAssure ReAssure 2.0 ReAssure 2.0\n\n**HNI** PREMIA\n\nReAssure 3.0 **was** launched in Q2'FY2026\n\n**HEALTH PLUS**\n\n**Product with \u201cIndustry-First\u201d Features**\n\n**MILLENNIALS**\n\n**was launched in Q2\u2019FY2026**\n\n**SENIOR CITIZEN**\n\n---\n\n## ReAssure 3.0 is Our Next Generation Retail Product with Several Customer Centric 2 and Innovative Product Features\n\n## ReAssuREX3.0 Go Limitless\n\n### Key Features\n\n##### No Cap on Sum Insured\n\n\u2022 Unlimited sum insured available \nwith all variants\n\n##### Vintage Pricing\n\n\u2022 Vintage as rating factor for \nexisting & port policies\n\n\u2022 Black: Any Room\n\n##### Room Category Basis Variants\n\n\u2022 Elite: Any Room except Deluxe/Suite\n\n\u2022 Select: Twin Sharing\n\n##### Options to make Premium affordable\n\n\u2022 HeadsUp, Tiered Network, Co-\nPayments & Deductible\n\n\u2022 Classic : General Ward\n\n##### Value Added Features\n\n\u2022 Wellconsult+: OPD Benefits upto INR 1Lac\n\n\u2022 Cashbag+: Earn cashback every year & \nuse it to pay for premiums.\n\n\u2022 Safeguard+: Pays for non-payable Items\n\n##### HNI Variant\n\n\u2022 Bordeless: Treatment anywhere in \nthe world up to 5Cr.\n\n\u2022 NivaBupaOne: Executive Health \nAssessment & Dedicated Support \nteam\n\n---\n\n## Enabling Access to a 360\u00b0 Health and Wellness Ecosystem Platform, Providing a 2 Holistic Customer Health Proposition\n\nApp Downloads\n(in Mn.)\n\n| Category | App Downloads (in Mn.) |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2024 | 2.3 |\n| FY2025 | 11.5 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 13.0 |\n\nMonthly Active Users (in Lacs)\n[Image: Image403]\n[Image: Image401]\n\n| Category | Monthly Active Users (in Lacs) |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2024 | 3.1 |\n| FY2025 | 5.1 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 5.8 |\n\nMonthly Average Health \nCheckups\n[Image: Image401] [Image: Image416]\n\n| Category | Monthly Average Health Checkups (k) |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2024 | 23 |\n| FY2025 | 38 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 51 |\n\nMonthly Average Doctor \nConsultation\n[Image: Image401] [Image: Image418]\n\n| Category | Monthly Average Doctor Consultation (k) |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2024 | 3.5 |\n| FY2025 | 6.3 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 6.7 |\n\nABC\nxxxxxxxxxx\n\n##### HEALTH OFFERINGS\n\nHome delivery of \nmedicines\n\nBooking individual \ndiagnostic tests with \nhome sample \ncollection\n\n##### WELLNESS OFFERINGS\n\n1\n\n$\n\n#\n\nActivity tracker\n\nCurated products \noffering discounts if \nminimum step count \nis achieved\n\nDigital consultations \nand second medical \nopinion\n\n+\n\nAccess health \neducation content \non diseases \npublished by Bupa \nand wellness content\n\nHealth assessment \ntools such as BMI and \nstress calculator\n\nHealthcare provider \nquality and \ninfrastructure matrix\n\n---\n\n## We Measure NPS Across 35 Touch Points and are Focused on Continuously 2 Improving Customer Experience\n\n**Weighted Episodal NPS 1**\n\n| Category | Weighted Episodal NPS |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 38 |\n| FY2024 | 50 |\n| FY2025 | 55 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 57 |\n\n| Category | Claims Cashless Discharge NPS |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 62 |\n| FY2024 | 63 |\n| FY2025 | 67 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 64 |\n\n\u25aa Weighted Episodal NPS for H1\u2019FY2026 stands at +57 which is +2 points higher than FY2025\n\n\u25aa 19 Lakh+ customers were reached out seeking feedback\n\n\u25aa 2 Lakh+ customer responses received\n\n###### Note:\n\n1. NPS score of few critical touch points (claims discharge, service, policy issuance, renewal etc.) is combined into a single, weighted \nNPS score, calculated as weighted average by response method, for the organisation\n\n---\n\n## 3 Multi-Channel & Diversified Distribution with Emphasis on Digital Sales\n\n<u><strong>Diversified Channel Mix with Strong Focus on Growing High Value Channels</strong></u>\n\n| Category | Individual Agents (%) | Corporate Agents - Banks (%) | Corporate Agents - Others (%) | Brokers(1) (%) | Direct Sale (%) | Others(2) (%) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2024 | 32.1 | 19.6 | 7.7 | 27.0 | 13.1 | 0.6 |\n| FY2025 | 29.7 | 20.1 | 7.5 | 30.6 | 11.5 | 0.6 |\n| H1'FY2025 | 30.1 | 20.8 | 8.7 | 27.2 | 12.7 | 0.5 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 30.6 | 19.8 | 10.5 | 28.0 | 10.5 | 0.6 |\n\n###### Notes:\n\n1. Brokers include PB Fintech (Policybazaar)\n\n2. Others include Web Aggregators,, Insurance Marketing Firms, Point of Sales and Common Service Centers\n\n<u><strong>Pan-India Presence</strong></u>\n\n**209** Branches\n\n**209,699** Individual Agents (+16K in Q2\u2019FY2026)\n[Image: Image440]\n[Image: Image436]\n\n**111** Banca & Other Corporate Agents (+12 in Q2\u2019FY2026)\n[Image: Image442]\n[Image: Image436]\n\n**563** Brokers (+19 in Q2\u2019FY2026)\n[Image: Image444]\n[Image: Image436]\n\n(3) (+574 in Q2\u2019FY2026)\n**9,834** Employees\n[Image: Image446] [Image: Image448]\n\n9,834 Employees (3) (+574 in Q2\u2019FY2026)\n\n3. On-roll employees\n\nMetrics as of H1'FY2026\n\nW.e.f. October 1, 2024 Long-term products are accounted on 1/n, as mandated by IRDAI, hence FY2025 & H1'FY2026 numbers are not comparable with prior periods\n\n---\n\n## Our Value Chain is Significantly Automated with Analytics Embedded into Operations\n\n###### Partner Onboarding\n\nModular API based\npartner integration\n\nDigital Dukaan and \nNiva Bupa UNO mobile \napplications for agent \ntraining\n\n###### Customer Sourcing\n\nNew policies applied \ndigitally\n\nPayments made \ndigitally\n\nReal-time lead scoring \nsupported by product \nrecommendation \nengine\n\n###### Underwriting\n\nRule based automated \ndecisioning\n\nRetail policies autodecisioned\n\nLTV-based approach to \nidentify upsell or crosssell opportunities\n\n###### Claims Management\n\nDigital claims submission\n\nReal-time fraud \ndetection capability\n\nOutlier detection tool \nused for billing review\n\nCashless Claims Auto-\nAdjudication\n\n###### Policy Renewal\n\nPolicy renewal without \nhuman intervention\n\nPredictive machinebased learning model \nto target high lapse \nprobability cases\n\n| Digital Metrics | FY2024 | FY2025 | H1'FY2025 | H1'FY2026 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| New policies applied via website and mobile apps | 100.0% | 99.9% | 99.9% | 99.9% |\n| Digital Payments | 95.5% | 95.1% | 96.6% | 96.2% |\n| Retail Policies auto-decisioned | 51.8% | 49.5% | 50.9% | 47.8% |\n| Claims submitted digitally | 81.3% | 91.5% | 90.1% | 91.6% |\n| Cashless claims auto adjudication | 19.8% | 27.3% | 31.0% | 12.5% |\n| Renewals completed without human intervention | 85.4% | 88.3% | 86.3% | 84.4% |\n| Cashless claims processed in <30 mins | 81.5% | 86.0% | 87.6% | 73.6% |\n\n**Note:** Cashless claims auto adjudication was on hold during Q1\u2019FY2026. Numbers are reported on exit basis\n\n---\n\n## 5 Disciplined Underwriting and Business Selection Through LTV-Based Approach\n\n## Product-to-customer, segment- PROFILE EXPERIENCE\n\n**COST OF** \n**ACQUISITION**\n\nCUSTOMER CLAIMS \nPROFILE EXPERIENCE\nLOCATION\nRISK PERCEPTION\nRETURN ON\n\n**MEDICAL** \n**INFLATION**\n\n**FUTURE**\n**PREMIUM**\n**CHANGE**\n\n**INVESTMENT**\n**INCOME**\n\n**REQUIRED**\n**CAPITAL**\n\n**DISTRIBUTION**\n**CHANNEL**\n\n**LTV-**\n**Based** \n**Scale**\n\n**COHORT-WISE** \n**LOSS RATIO**\n\n**Rating**\n\n**Follow-Up** \n**Action**\n\n## Action RISK PERCEPTION\nSignificant Over Index LTV-\n\n###### Significant\n\n**Product-to-customer, segmentto-channel mapping**\n[Image: Image465]\n\n###### Decision Vectors\n\n**Identify opportunities** for upsell \nor cross-sell to customers with \nhigh LTV\n[Image: Image465]\n\n**Customized** and pre-qualified \noffers for each customer\n[Image: Image465]\n\n**Sales channel alignment** of\n\nincentives and monthly review \nto increase renewals\n[Image: Image465]\n\nUse **differentiated interventions**\n\nto maximize customer retention\n[Image: Image465]\n\n---\n\n## 5 Our Multi-Pronged Claims Management Strategy\n\n1 **Developing Partnerships and Strengthening Relationships with Network Hospitals**\nExpansion of Network of Preferred Partner Network (PPN) Hospitals\n\n2 **Auto Adjudication**\nPaperless Auto Adjudication Portal for Health Insurance Claims Processing\n\n3 **Robust Fraud Detection**\nReal Time Detection of Outliers in Claims Based on Disease, Treatment Provider, Location And Policy Seller\n\n4 **Billing Review**\nRandom Checks and Case-Specific Triggers to Identify Anomalies\n\n5 **Case Management**\nCost Component Review on a Claim-by-Claim Basis with Medical Providers\n\n---\n\n## Our Hospital Network and PPN Hospitals Helps Improve Customer Satisfaction 5 Levels While Improving Control on Cost of Claims\n\n<u><strong>Network of Hospitals (#)</strong></u>\n\n| Category | Network of Hospitals (#) |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2022 | 8562 |\n| FY2023 | 10005 |\n| FY2024 | 10460 |\n| FY2025 | 10421 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 10507 |\n\n<u><strong>Preferred Partner Network (#)</strong></u>\n\n| Category | Series 1 (unlabelled) (#) | Preferred Partner Network Live in Cities (#) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2023 | 201 | 9 |\n| FY2024 | 326 | 20 |\n| FY2025 | 589 | 40 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 855 | 44 |\n\nPreferred Partner Network Live in Cities (#)\n\n#### Benefits of PPN Hospitals\n\n#### For Customers\n\nPPN claims \ncontribution in \nPPN cities ~19%\n\nFree ambulance \nservices and \ndesignated \nrelationship manager\n\nDiscount on \npharmacy, diagnostics \nand consultations \neven after discharge\n\nFavourable discount \npackages, controlling \ncost of claims\n\n#### For Niva Bupa\n\nImproved \n[Image: Image493]transparency of billing\n\n---\n\n## 5 Retail Health Claims Cost Index\n\n<u><strong>Our Retail Health Claims Cost Index<sup>1</sup> has grown by a CAGR<sup>2</sup> of 7.0%</strong></u>\n\n| Category | Retail Health Claims Cost Index (FY2019 = 100) |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2019 | 100 |\n| FY2020 | 101 |\n| FY2021 | 123 |\n| FY2022 | 128 |\n| FY2023 | 131 |\n| FY2024 | 141 |\n| FY2025 | 152 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 155 |\n\n**Retail Health Claim Cost Index reflects YOY average claim size with FY2019 as base year. The change in index is on \naccount of medical cost inflation, change in disease mix, medical advancement etc.** \n[Image: Image503]\n[Image: Image501]\n\n---\n\n**6 Focus on Talent Management & Execution**\n\n**2021**\n\nGreat Place To Work\u00ae\n\nCertified\n\nFEB 2021-JAN 2022\n\nINDIA\n\n**2022**\n\nGreat Place To Work.\n\nBest Workplaces\n\n**2023**\n\nGreat Place To Work.\n\nGreat Place To Work.\n\n**2024**\n\nGreat Place To Work.\n\nGreat Place To Work.\n\nBest Workplaces in General & Health Insurance\n\nBest Workplaces\n\nTHE ECONOMIC TIMES\n\nGreat Place To Work.\n\nBest Workplaces\n\n**Top 25 India\u2019s Best** \nWorkplaces<sup>TM</sup>\n**in BFSI 2025**\n\n## Workplaces TM\n\n**2025**\n\nin Health and Wellness\n\nTHE ECONOMIC TIMES\n\nRanked 67<sup>th</sup> among Top 100 India\u2019s Best \nWorkplaces<sup>TM</sup> 2025\n\nBest Workplaces in General & Health Insurance\n\n---\n\n## Agenda\n\nOur Strategy\n\nFinancial Performance\n\n---\n\n## Financial Performance (IFRS)\n\n**Profit After Tax (PAT)**\n\n**Key Ratios**\n\n| Category | Profit After Tax (PAT) (\u20b9 in Crores) |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2024 | 106.4 |\n| FY2025 | 202.9 |\n| H1'FY2025 | 59.5 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 131.7 |\n\n| Category | Retail Claims Ratio (%) | Combined Insurance Service Ratio (%) | Expense Ratio (%) | Claims Ratio (%) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2024 | 64.8 | 103.0 | 40.1 | 62.9 |\n| FY2025 | 66.0 | 103.0 | 39.2 | 63.8 |\n| H1'FY2025 | 68.0 | 104.2 | 39.5 | 64.7 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 68.1 | 103.1 | 37.2 | 65.9 |\n\n---\n\n## Financial Performance (I-GAAP)\n\n**Profit/Loss After Tax**\n\n*(\u20b9 in Crores)*\n\n| Category | Profit/Loss After Tax (\u20b9 in Crores) |\n| --- | --- |\n| FY2024 | 81.9 |\n| FY2025 | 213.5 |\n| H1'FY2025 | -5.8 |\n| H1'FY2026 | -126.7 |\n\n**Key Ratios**\n\n| Category | Claims Ratio (%) | Expense Ratio (%) | Combined Ratio (%) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2024 | 59.0 | 39.8 | 98.8 |\n| FY2025 | 61.2 | 40.0 | 101.2 |\n| H1'FY2025 | 62.5 | 41.0 | 103.5 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 74.3 | 39.9 | 114.1 |\n| H1'FY2026 Without 1/n | 69.1 | 37.1 | 106.2 |\n\n---\n\n# I-GAAP Claims Ratio Bridge\n\n1 2\n\n\u00b9Driven by Group loss ratio. Two large corporate accounts were written in Q4\u2019FY2025 so no corresponding earnings in H1\u2019FY2026 due to 50% UPR accounting & earnings will reflect in Q4\u2019FY2026 \u00b2W.e.f. October 1, 2024 Long-term products are accounted on 1/n, as mandated by IRDAI, hence H1'FY2026 earnings are lower due to 50% UPR accounting method\n\n| Category | Claims ratio (%) |\n| --- | --- |\n| H1'FY2025 | 62.5 |\n| Impact of Group Business | 6.7 |\n| H1'FY2026 (Without 1/n) | 69.1 |\n| Impact of 1/n Accounting | 5.2 |\n| H1'FY2026 (With 1/n) | 74.3 |\n\n---\n\n## Profit Reconciliation from I-GAAP to IFRS\n\n| Particulars ( \u20b9 in Crores) | FY2024 | FY2025 | H1'FY2025 | H1'FY2026 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Profit After Taxes as per I-GAAP | 81.9 | 213.5 | (5.8) | (126.7) |\n| IFRS Adjustments |  |  |  |  |\n| Insurance Contracts [IFRS-17] | 68.7 | 80.8 | 96.5 | 304.9 |\n| Leases [IFRS-16] | (3.0) | (2.0) | (0.7) | (1.5) |\n| Financial Instruments [IFRS-09] | 3.5 | (4.0) | (0.7) | 9.7 |\n| Share-based Payment [IFRS-02] | (8.8) | (13.7) | (7.2) | (9.1) |\n| Employee Benefits [IAS-19] | 0.7 | 1.4 | 0.9 | 2.5 |\n| Income Taxes [IAS-12] | (36.6) | (73.1) | (23.4) | (48.0) |\n| Profit After Taxes as per IFRS | 106.4 | 202.9 | 59.5 | 131.7 |\n\n---\n\n## Equity Reconciliation from I-GAAP to IFRS\n\n| Particulars ( \u20b9 in Crores) | As at March 31, 2024 | As at March 31, 2025 | As at Sep 30, 2024 | As at Sep 30, 2025 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Equity as per I-GAAP | 2,049.8 | 3,060.8 | 2,064.6 | 2,956.0 |\n| IFRS Adjustments |  |  |  |  |\n| Insurance Contracts [IFRS-17] | 111.4 | 192.3 | 208.0 | 497.2 |\n| Leases [IFRS-16] | (2.2) | (4.2) | (2.9) | (5.8) |\n| Financial Instruments [IFRS-09] | (11.3) | 93.9 | 35.2 | 122.2 |\n| Income Taxes [IAS-12] | 49.9 | (50.4) | 28.4 | (102.4) |\n| Equity as per IFRS | 2,197.5 | 3,292.4 | 2,333.2 | 3,467.1 |\n\n---\n\n## Robust Approach to Investment Management has Resulted in Strong Growth in AUM and Yield\n\n**AUM** (\u20b9 in Crores)\n\n| Category | AUM (\u20b9 in Crores) | Investment Yield\u00b9 (%) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| FY2022 | 2401.3 | 6.6 |\n| FY2023 | 3366.1 | 6.7 |\n| FY2024 | 5458.2 | 7.1 |\n| FY2025 | 8175.1 | 7.4 |\n| H1'FY2026 | 8481.8 | 7.3 |\n\n###### Note:\n\n1. Investment yield is annualized for H1'FY2026\n\n**Breakup by Ratings**\n% of Book Value of Debt Securities| H1'FY2026\n\n| Category | Share (%) |\n| --- | --- |\n| AAA Rated | 60.7 |\n| AA / AA+ | 7.9 |\n| Sovereign | 31.4 |\n\n---\n\nAppendix\n\n---\n\n## Glossary\n\n**API** - Application Programming Interface\n\n**App** - Application\n\n**AUM** - Assets under Management\n\n**Avg** - Average\n\n**BMI** - Body Mass Index\n\n**CAGR** - Compounded Annual Growth Rate\n\n**EOM** - Expense of Management\n\n**Excl** - Excluding\n\n**FY** - Financial Year\n\n**GDPI** - Gross Direct Premium Income\n\n**GWP** - Gross Written Premium\n\n**HNI** - High Net worth Individuals\n\n**IFRS** - International Financial Reporting Standards\n\n**I-GAAP** -Indian Generally Accepted Accounting Principles\n\n**LTV** - Life Time Value\n\n**MAU** - Monthly Active Users\n\n**Mn** - Million\n\n**NBFC** - Non-Banking Financial Company\n\n**NWP** - Net Written Premium\n\n**NEP** - Net Earned Premium\n\n**NPS** - Net Promoter Score\n\n**PA** - Personal Accident\n\n**PAT** - Profit After Tax\n\n**PB** - Policy Bazaar\n\n**PBT** - Profit Before Tax\n\n**PPN** - Preferred Partner Network\n\n**RBI** - Reserve Bank of India\n\n**RI** - Reinsurance\n\n**ROAE** - Returnon Average Equity\n\n**\u20b9** - Indian Rupees\n\n---\n\n## Thank You"}}, "step6_WebReader3": {"step": 6, "title": "Content from https://transactions.nivabupa.com/pages/doc/investor-relations/Corporate-Announcements/2025-26/Certificate-Regulation-quarter-ended-September-2025.pdf?v=1.1", "toolName": "WebReader", "url": "https://transactions.nivabupa.com/pages/doc/investor-relations/Corporate-Announcements/2025-26/Certificate-Regulation-quarter-ended-September-2025.pdf?v=1.1", "snippet": "October 13, 2025\n\nRef: NIVABUPA/EQ/2025-26/61\n\nTo, \n**National Stock Exchange of India Limited** \nExchange Plaza, C-1, Block G \nBandra Kurla Complex \nBandra (E), Mumbai \u2013 400 051 \n**Symbol : NIVABUPA**\n\n## BSE Limited\n\nPhiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers \nDalal Street, Mumbai \u2013 400 001\n\n## Scrip Code: 544286\n...", "raw_data": {"content_markdown": "October 13, 2025\n\nRef: NIVABUPA/EQ/2025-26/61\n\nTo, \n**National Stock Exchange of India Limited** \nExchange Plaza, C-1, Block G \nBandra Kurla Complex \nBandra (E), Mumbai \u2013 400 051 \n**Symbol : NIVABUPA**\n\n## BSE Limited\n\nPhiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers \nDalal Street, Mumbai \u2013 400 001\n\n## Scrip Code: 544286\n\n**Sub: Certificate pursuant to Regulation 74(5) of SEBI (Depositories and Participants) Regulations, 2018 \nfor the quarter ended September 30, 2025**\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nPursuant to Regulation 74(5) of SEBI (Depositories and Participants) Regulations, 